{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792859325837,"sessionID":"ses_e9141cfbdffenLAFgwFuHpfkdd","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_02_TpVKe8l8kBuEuShIWopJ4626","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"C:\\src\\m0saic-production\\one-a-day\\journal\\2026-10-24\\40-critique.md"},"output":"<path>C:\\src\\m0saic-production\\one-a-day\\journal\\2026-10-24\\40-critique.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Critique — 2026-10-24\n2: \n3: ## Scores\n4: \n5: | variant | 1 | 2 | 3 | 4 | 5 | 6 | 7 | 8 | 9 | total | fatal? |\n6: |---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n7: | a | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 18 | no |\n8: | b | 2 | 1 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 17 | no |\n9: \n10: Judged without image input (this model cannot read the PNGs). Verified against\n11: `report.json` (all renders exit 0, `degraded:false`), `node tools/check-registry.mjs\n12: --json` (clean for this template; the two warnings there are pre-existing on other\n13: templates), the flattened `.layout.m0`, the full `src`, both test files, and a\n14: pixel-level probe of the rendered PNGs (header/body carry 82/139 unique colours and\n15: the hero \"45:02\" bbox is anti-aliased digits, not a filled box — so the engine's\n16: `OVERLAY_CHAIN_DEEP` (45) warning does not manifest as tofu text here).\n17: \n18: ## What each variant gets right / wrong\n19: \n20: **a (primary) — bar = split, pink = mistake**\n21: - Right: renders clean at landscape/portrait/square and all seven contract canvases\n22:   at defaults; footer is honest arithmetic — `TIME W/O MISTAKES 42:04`, `TOTAL LOSS\n23:   +2:58`, `BEST LEG 1:32` = finish 45:02 − Σloss 2:58, exactly three pink legs (1, 5,\n24:   9) with signed loss, clean legs leave the loss cell blank.\n25: - Right: finish is the largest text at every aspect (118px@1920 → 29px@480); header/\n26:   body/footer hold their 0–0.26 / 0.26–0.80 / 0.80–1 bands; tape rail is 34% ≥ 32%;\n27:   rows and the three footer cells are equal-height, all per the declared contract.\n28: - Weak: no column header row — a stranger must infer that the bold column is the\n29:   split and the pink signed column is the loss; only the `+` and the pink carry the\n30:   distinction. Reads fine, but it leans hard on the \"no legend\" promise.\n31: \n32: **b (loss-first)**\n33: - Right: same clean render, same contract, same footer; the pink left rule + wash\n34:   make the three mistake rows unmistakable and the loss is the bold figure exactly\n35:   as the brief's \"loss-first\" asked.\n36: - Wrong: dimming the split severs the \"bar length = split\" link the rubric's line 2\n37:   depends on — the number that explains the tape is now secondary, so the card reads\n38:   \"pink rows\" before \"where the minutes went\".\n39: - Weak: the pink wash on the whole mistake row adds a second accent hue to the tape\n40:   track, slightly muddying the clean pink=bar mapping; same missing column header.\n41: \n42: ## Decision: SHIP a\n43: \n44: ## What a human polish pass should look at first\n45: \n46: 1. **WHY.timeline is stale** — it lists only scout(+2 retries) and plan; the build\n47:    phase (≈40 min, the phase that actually produced the template) is absent from\n48:    `tutorial-6`. Regenerate in the ship phase\n49:    (`node pipeline/lib/trace.mjs --timeline journal/2026-10-24/trace.json`) and copy\n50:    into `WHY.timeline` before the runner freezes it. Not fatal — the ship loop owns it.\n51: 2. **`OVERLAY_CHAIN_DEEP` (45 deep)** — engine warning, text verified rendering, but\n52:    it is over the ~25 comfort ceiling. Record-posture: a future pass could nest the\n53:    tape band into a child doc to cut depth. Do not chase it today.\n54: 3. **The \"iof-xml\" tag over-promises** — the template takes a JSON `splits` list whose\n55:    field names mirror IOF XML 3.0; it does not parse XML. The description (\"from one\n56:    IOF XML 3.0 result row\") is one step past what is true. A lone racer must transcribe\n57:    13 legs by hand; the batch use case (a club's timing system scripting the props) is\n58:    where this earns its keep, and that converter is out of scope.\n59: \n60: ## If no ship: the one thing that would have changed the verdict\n61: \n62: (n/a — shipping a.) For the record, the thing closest to sinking it was the missing\n63: column header combined with the manual-JSON-only input: if either the split/loss\n64: columns were unlabeled *and* the input were not batchable, this would be a no-ship.\n65: The footer math, the fail-fast validation, and the honest layout contract are what\n66: carried it over the line.\n\n(End of file - total 66 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Critique — 2026-10-24\n\n## Scores\n\n| variant | 1 | 2 | 3 | 4 | 5 | 6 | 7 | 8 | 9 | total | fatal? |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| a | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 18 | no |\n| b | 2 | 1 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 17 | no |\n\nJudged without image input (this model cannot read the PNGs). Verified against\n`report.json` (all renders exit 0, `degraded:false`), `node tools/check-registry.mjs\n--json` (clean for this template; the two warnings there are pre-existing on other\ntemplates), the flattened `.layout.m0`, the full `src`, both test files, and a\npixel-level probe of the rendered PNGs (header/body carry 82/139 unique colours and\nthe hero \"45:02\" bbox is anti-aliased digits, not a filled box — so the engine's\n`OVERLAY_CHAIN_DEEP` (45) warning does not manifest as tofu text here).\n\n## What each variant gets right / wrong\n\n**a (primary) — bar = split, pink = mistake**","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"C:\\src\\m0saic-production\\one-a-day\\journal\\2026-10-24\\40-critique.md","text":"# Critique — 2026-10-24\n\n## Scores\n\n| variant | 1 | 2 | 3 | 4 | 5 | 6 | 7 | 8 | 9 | total | fatal? |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| a | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 18 | no |\n| b | 2 | 1 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 17 | no |\n\nJudged without image input (this model cannot read the PNGs). Verified against\n`report.json` (all renders exit 0, `degraded:false`), `node tools/check-registry.mjs\n--json` (clean for this template; the two warnings there are pre-existing on other\ntemplates), the flattened `.layout.m0`, the full `src`, both test files, and a\npixel-level probe of the rendered PNGs (header/body carry 82/139 unique colours and\nthe hero \"45:02\" bbox is anti-aliased digits, not a filled box — so the engine's\n`OVERLAY_CHAIN_DEEP` (45) warning does not manifest as tofu text here).\n\n## What each variant gets right / wrong\n\n**a (primary) — bar = split, pink = mistake**\n- Right: renders clean at landscape/portrait/square and all seven contract canvases\n  at defaults; footer is honest arithmetic — `TIME W/O MISTAKES 42:04`, `TOTAL LOSS\n  +2:58`, `BEST LEG 1:32` = finish 45:02 − Σloss 2:58, exactly three pink legs (1, 5,\n  9) with signed loss, clean legs leave the loss cell blank.\n- Right: finish is the largest text at every aspect (118px@1920 → 29px@480); header/\n  body/footer hold their 0–0.26 / 0.26–0.80 / 0.80–1 bands; tape rail is 34% ≥ 32%;\n  rows and the three footer cells are equal-height, all per the declared contract.\n- Weak: no column header row — a stranger must infer that the bold column is the\n  split and the pink signed column is the loss; only the `+` and the pink carry the\n  distinction. Reads fine, but it leans hard on the \"no legend\" promise.\n\n**b (loss-first)**\n- Right: same clean render, same contract, same footer; the pink left rule + wash\n  make the three mistake rows unmistakable and the loss is the bold figure exactly\n  as the brief's \"loss-first\" asked.\n- Wrong: dimming the split severs the \"bar length = split\" link the rubric's line 2\n  depends on — the number that explains the tape is now secondary, so the card reads\n  \"pink rows\" before \"where the minutes went\".\n- Weak: the pink wash on the whole mistake row adds a second accent hue to the tape\n  track, slightly muddying the clean pink=bar mapping; same missing column header.\n\n## Decision: SHIP a\n\n## What a human polish pass should look at first\n\n1. **WHY.timeline is stale** — it lists only scout(+2 retries) and plan; the build\n   phase (≈40 min, the phase that actually produced the template) is absent from\n   `tutorial-6`. Regenerate in the ship phase\n   (`node pipeline/lib/trace.mjs --timeline journal/2026-10-24/trace.json`) and copy\n   into `WHY.timeline` before the runner freezes it. Not fatal — the ship loop owns it.\n2. **`OVERLAY_CHAIN_DEEP` (45 deep)** — engine warning, text verified rendering, but\n   it is over the ~25 comfort ceiling. Record-posture: a future pass could nest the\n   tape band into a child doc to cut depth. Do not chase it today.\n3. **The \"iof-xml\" tag over-promises** — the template takes a JSON `splits` list whose\n   field names mirror IOF XML 3.0; it does not parse XML. The description (\"from one\n   IOF XML 3.0 result row\") is one step past what is true. A lone racer must transcribe\n   13 legs by hand; the batch use case (a club's timing system scripting the props) is\n   where this earns its keep, and that converter is out of scope.\n\n## If no ship: the one thing that would have changed the verdict\n\n(n/a — shipping a.) For the record, the thing closest to sinking it was the missing\ncolumn header combined with the manual-JSON-only input: if either the split/loss\ncolumns were unlabeled *and* the input were not batchable, this would be a no-ship.\nThe footer math, the fail-fast validation, and the honest layout contract are what\ncarried it over the line.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":66,"totalLines":66,"truncated":false}},"title":"journal\\2026-10-24\\40-critique.md","time":{"start":1792859325820,"end":1792859325835}},"id":"prt_16ebe4483001I5JGHJiQH8hcH0","sessionID":"ses_e9141cfbdffenLAFgwFuHpfkdd","messageID":"msg_16ebe3215001QvDkq2ngROxg2C"}}
