{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792859329606,"sessionID":"ses_e9141cfbdffenLAFgwFuHpfkdd","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_00_7URTHirHgJqvuFHXxaNX8155","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"C:\\src\\m0saic-production\\one-a-day\\journal\\2026-10-24\\30-build.md"},"output":"<path>C:\\src\\m0saic-production\\one-a-day\\journal\\2026-10-24\\30-build.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Build — 2026-10-24\n2: \n3: ## Template: @one-a-day/sports/orienteering-split-analysis/v1\n4: \n5: One racer's IOF XML 3.0 result row as a shareable split-analysis card. Finish time is\n6: the hero with course and place beside it; each leg is a tape whose length is\n7: `split / slowest`, and any leg with time loss (`loss > 0`, the WinSplits per-leg number)\n8: is pink in bar and signed loss text. Footer computes `TIME W/O MISTAKES = finish - sum(loss)`,\n9: `TOTAL LOSS = sum(loss)`, `BEST LEG = min(split)` from the entered numbers only.\n10: \n11: ## Variant a — bar = split, pink = mistake · gate: clean · render: ok · stills: layout-verified\n12: \n13: The primary. Dark card, split tape whose length is the split over the slowest leg, mistake\n14: legs pink (bar + signed loss text), clean legs neutral with a blank loss cell. No legend.\n15: \n16: - Build gate clean for this template (the two warnings in the log are pre-existing on\n17:   `@one-a-day/dev/og-card/v1` and `@one-a-day/social/episode-audiogram/v1`, not mine).\n18: - Rendered landscape/portrait/square all exit 0, not degraded; tutorial 6 pages exit 0.\n19: - **I could not open the PNG stills** (this model does not take image input). I verified\n20:   every claim against the flattened layout instead: hero is the largest text at all five\n21:   canvases (118px @1920, 79px @1280, 178px @1080x1920, 117px @1080x1080, 29px @480x270);\n22:   header cells all end above y=0.26, body rows sit in [0.26, 0.80], footer in [0.80, 1];\n23:   tape rail is 0.34 W (>= 0.32); exactly 3/13 bars accent; clean legs have no loss cell;\n24:   footer reads `42:04 / +2:58 / 1:32`.\n25: \n26: ## Variant b — loss-first · gate: clean · render: ok\n27: \n28: One change from a: the time-loss column becomes the emphasised figure — split time dims\n29: (dim, not bold), the loss text goes bold accent, and the whole mistake row gets a thin\n30: pink left rule plus a pink wash. Rendered clean at all canvases and passes the test suite.\n31: It loses the \"split is the bold number\" default read, so it stays out of place.\n32: \n33: ## Why-tutorial\n34: \n35: - Problem page: quotes the WinSplits help line (\"Some split times have pink background\n36:   colour... a mistake has probably been made\") and notes that analysis lives in a table\n37:   page nobody can post, so orienteers hand-make the World of O plot.\n38: - Solution page: states the one decision — time loss is a prop, never re-derived — and that\n39:   the finish is printed as entered, never checked against the split sum.\n40: \n41: ## What was hard\n42: \n43: - The three pinned bands (0-0.26 / 0.26-0.80 / 0.80-1) leave only ~141px for the body at\n44:   480x270, so 13 legs squeeze to a 6px floor and 18 legs fail-fast there (fits everywhere\n45:   else). The `club · class` line had to split into two bound cells to avoid a `bindingsCover`\n46:   warning on `className`, and the cell widths needed the `/0.94` margin or `textFitsMeasured`\n47:   flagged a <1px clip.\n48: \n49: ## In place now: a\n\n(End of file - total 49 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Build — 2026-10-24\n\n## Template: @one-a-day/sports/orienteering-split-analysis/v1\n\nOne racer's IOF XML 3.0 result row as a shareable split-analysis card. Finish time is\nthe hero with course and place beside it; each leg is a tape whose length is\n`split / slowest`, and any leg with time loss (`loss > 0`, the WinSplits per-leg number)\nis pink in bar and signed loss text. Footer computes `TIME W/O MISTAKES = finish - sum(loss)`,\n`TOTAL LOSS = sum(loss)`, `BEST LEG = min(split)` from the entered numbers only.\n\n## Variant a — bar = split, pink = mistake · gate: clean · render: ok · stills: layout-verified\n\nThe primary. Dark card, split tape whose length is the split over the slowest leg, mistake\nlegs pink (bar + signed loss text), clean legs neutral with a blank loss cell. No legend.\n\n- Build gate clean for this template (the two warnings in the log are pre-existing on\n  `@one-a-day/dev/og-card/v1` and `@one-a-day/social/episode-audiogram/v1`, not mine).\n- Rendered landscape/portrait/square all exit 0, not degraded; tutorial 6 pages exit 0.\n- **I could not open the PNG stills** (this model does not take image input). I verified\n  every claim against the flattened layout instead: hero is the largest text at all five","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"C:\\src\\m0saic-production\\one-a-day\\journal\\2026-10-24\\30-build.md","text":"# Build — 2026-10-24\n\n## Template: @one-a-day/sports/orienteering-split-analysis/v1\n\nOne racer's IOF XML 3.0 result row as a shareable split-analysis card. Finish time is\nthe hero with course and place beside it; each leg is a tape whose length is\n`split / slowest`, and any leg with time loss (`loss > 0`, the WinSplits per-leg number)\nis pink in bar and signed loss text. Footer computes `TIME W/O MISTAKES = finish - sum(loss)`,\n`TOTAL LOSS = sum(loss)`, `BEST LEG = min(split)` from the entered numbers only.\n\n## Variant a — bar = split, pink = mistake · gate: clean · render: ok · stills: layout-verified\n\nThe primary. Dark card, split tape whose length is the split over the slowest leg, mistake\nlegs pink (bar + signed loss text), clean legs neutral with a blank loss cell. No legend.\n\n- Build gate clean for this template (the two warnings in the log are pre-existing on\n  `@one-a-day/dev/og-card/v1` and `@one-a-day/social/episode-audiogram/v1`, not mine).\n- Rendered landscape/portrait/square all exit 0, not degraded; tutorial 6 pages exit 0.\n- **I could not open the PNG stills** (this model does not take image input). I verified\n  every claim against the flattened layout instead: hero is the largest text at all five\n  canvases (118px @1920, 79px @1280, 178px @1080x1920, 117px @1080x1080, 29px @480x270);\n  header cells all end above y=0.26, body rows sit in [0.26, 0.80], footer in [0.80, 1];\n  tape rail is 0.34 W (>= 0.32); exactly 3/13 bars accent; clean legs have no loss cell;\n  footer reads `42:04 / +2:58 / 1:32`.\n\n## Variant b — loss-first · gate: clean · render: ok\n\nOne change from a: the time-loss column becomes the emphasised figure — split time dims\n(dim, not bold), the loss text goes bold accent, and the whole mistake row gets a thin\npink left rule plus a pink wash. Rendered clean at all canvases and passes the test suite.\nIt loses the \"split is the bold number\" default read, so it stays out of place.\n\n## Why-tutorial\n\n- Problem page: quotes the WinSplits help line (\"Some split times have pink background\n  colour... a mistake has probably been made\") and notes that analysis lives in a table\n  page nobody can post, so orienteers hand-make the World of O plot.\n- Solution page: states the one decision — time loss is a prop, never re-derived — and that\n  the finish is printed as entered, never checked against the split sum.\n\n## What was hard\n\n- The three pinned bands (0-0.26 / 0.26-0.80 / 0.80-1) leave only ~141px for the body at\n  480x270, so 13 legs squeeze to a 6px floor and 18 legs fail-fast there (fits everywhere\n  else). The `club · class` line had to split into two bound cells to avoid a `bindingsCover`\n  warning on `className`, and the cell widths needed the `/0.94` margin or `textFitsMeasured`\n  flagged a <1px clip.\n\n## In place now: a","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":49,"totalLines":49,"truncated":false}},"title":"journal\\2026-10-24\\30-build.md","time":{"start":1792859329589,"end":1792859329603}},"id":"prt_16ebe5348001YH2xFez7Ai67un","sessionID":"ses_e9141cfbdffenLAFgw